# Docker's ignore patterns are anchored to the build context root unless they
# start with "**", so a bare ".next" only matches ./.next — it does NOT match
# apps/web-ui/.next. Left unanchored that stale build output is 446 MB of the
# context, and it also shadows the directory the Dockerfile builds into.
**/node_modules
.git
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/dist
**/.next
**/.source
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.DS_Store
coverage
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
*~
